From 339dcf9e9d5ee6eda97a44dc686014f0779d2d14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Leto <anthony@as393941.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:50:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] core: identify a known device by its libusb_device, not its
 address alone

usb_find_devices() treated any device on a bus with a known address as
the device already in the list. A device that re-enumerates between two
scans usually gets the same address back, and libusb-1.0 then hands out
a new libusb_device for it; the old entry kept pointing at the detached
object, so every later usb_open() failed with LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE
until the process exited.

Seen with pilot-link polling a Palm handheld on macOS: the handheld
re-enumerates when HotSync is tapped, and the listener was stuck on
"could not open device, error -4" for the rest of its life.

Require the same libusb_device as well as the same address before
treating an entry as unchanged. On platforms where libusb-1.0 keeps one
object per attached device this changes nothing.
---
 libusb/core.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libusb/core.c b/libusb/core.c
index 9b1527b..5cdf857 100644
--- a/libusb/core.c
+++ b/libusb/core.c
@@ -656,7 +656,16 @@ API_EXPORTED int usb_find_devices(void)
 			struct usb_device *ndev = new_devices;
 
 			while (ndev) {
-				if (ndev->devnum == dev->devnum) {
+				/* The address alone does not identify a device. One that
+				 * re-enumerates between two scans (a Palm handheld switching
+				 * modes, or recovering from a stall) usually gets its old
+				 * address back, and libusb-1.0 then hands out a new
+				 * libusb_device for it. Keeping our old entry would leave
+				 * callers with a device that can never be opened again
+				 * (LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_DEVICE), so only a match on the underlying
+				 * libusb_device counts as the same device; otherwise the old
+				 * one is reported removed and the new one added. */
+				if (ndev->devnum == dev->devnum && ndev->dev == dev->dev) {
 					LIST_DEL(new_devices, ndev);
 					free(ndev);
 					found = 1;
-- 
